(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The limited C API's remainder (queue 268; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 268\"): the functions of queue 262's"] [4 1 "// list of natives not provided (`.tmp/q262/missing.txt`) that the world's _testlimitedcapi reaches and pyi's objects"] [5 1 "// answer directly: dicts, sets, lists, tuples, ints, floats, complex numbers, bytes, bytearrays, the number, mapping"] [6 1 "// and sequence protocols, str's core, weak references, imports' module table, PyMem. Each follows its CPython 3.14.10"] [7 1 "// definition (Objects/dictobject.c, setobject.c, listobject.c, tupleobject.c, longobject.c, floatobject.c,"] [8 1 "// complexobject.c, bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c, abstract.c, unicodeobject.c, weakrefobject.c, Python/import.c,"] [9 1 "// Objects/obmalloc.c): the type checks and their messages, the operation through pyi's own (its type's method or"] [10 1 "// protocol, as CPython's calls the type's slot). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [24 1 "// callMeth calls o's method name with args."] [33 1 "// each calls f on each item of iter(o) until it returns an error (Iterate's)."] [41 1 "// callBuiltin calls builtins.name with args."] [50 1 "// opArgs are a native's object arguments, nil for NULL; err when one is NULL (null_error)."] [70 1 "// bigOf is o as an int (its __index__), CPython's _PyNumber_Index."] [82 1 "// asUnsigned is PyLong_AsUnsignedLong's family: o an int (no __index__), in [0, 2**bits)."] [101 1 "// asSignedBits is PyLong_AsInt32's family: o's __index__ in the signed range of bits."] [113 1 "// unsignedIndex is PyLong_AsUInt32's family: o's __index__ in [0, 2**bits)."] [130 1 "// storeInt writes the int v of size bytes at p (an output argument), when p is not NULL."] [147 2 "// ---- dicts (Objects/dictobject.c) ----"] [150 70 "// PyDict_Check: a subclass's instance too"] [188 34 "// _PyErr_SetKeyError"] [212 2 "// PyDict_GetItem and GetItemString: borrowed, errors suppressed; an error but KeyError (an unhashable key, a key that"] [213 2 "// does not decode) reported as unraisable (dictobject.c's dict_getitem, PyErr_FormatUnraisable)"] [238 21 "// _PyObject_HashFast's error, not the lookup's"] [304 2 "// PyDict_Next(d, Py_ssize_t *pos, PyObject **key, PyObject **value): borrowed references"] [349 2 "// ---- sets (Objects/setobject.c) ----"] [375 3 "// set_contains_key: the key hashed as is (set's `in` retries an unhashable set as a frozenset; PySet_Contains not)"] [401 4 "// a brand new frozenset (C holds its only reference: PyFrozenSet_New's) is filled in place"] [409 4 "// _PyErr_BadInternalCall(__FILE__, __LINE__) of Objects/setobject.c's PySet_Add (a frozenset too: pyi's are"] [410 4 "// never brand new to C)"] [437 2 "// ---- lists and tuples (Objects/listobject.c, tupleobject.c) ----"] [535 2 "// ---- ints (Objects/longobject.c) ----"] [565 2 "// PyLong_FromVoidPtr: a pointer that is an object's handle keeps the handle (a reference the process keeps), so that"] [566 2 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr gives the same object back while Python holds it (a handle C no longer references is released)"] [591 2 "// longobject.c's messages, as they are"] [604 2 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr: an int (no __index__: \"an integer is required\") as a pointer; NULL on an error"] [638 2 "// PyLong_AsInt32 (o, int32_t *out) and the family: 0, or -1 with an error"] [643 24 "// *value left as it was"] [659 2 "// ---- floats and complex numbers ----"] [665 3 "// a str or a buffer only (Objects/floatobject.c; queue 270): float() also takes numbers"] [684 3 "// a new sys.float_info (floatobject.c's PyFloat_GetInfo makes one each call)"] [694 2 "// PyComplex_RealAsDouble and ImagAsDouble: capi_tail.go (asCComplex)"] [695 2 "// ---- the number protocol (Objects/abstract.c) ----"] [725 2 "// ---- the mapping and sequence protocols ----"] [760 2 "// the string-keyed forms (Objects/abstract.c): a NULL object or key is null_error's SystemError, the key decoded as"] [761 2 "// PyUnicode_FromString decodes it (its UnicodeDecodeError propagates)"] [795 2 "// PyMapping_HasKey and the rest: PyMapping_GetOptionalItem's lookup, a KeyError alone meaning absent (an IndexError"] [796 2 "// propagates); the forms without WithError report any error as unraisable, by their own message, and give 0"] [953 2 "// ---- bytes and bytearrays (Objects/bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c) ----"] [961 2 "// PyBytes_Repr(o, smartquotes) (Objects/bytesobject.c): double quotes only when smartquotes and the bytes hold a"] [962 2 "// single quote and no double quote; else single quotes, a single quote escaped"] [1006 47 "// the mirror's ob_sval (queue 269)"] [1014 2 "// PyBytes_Concat and PyBytes_ConcatAndDel (Objects/bytesobject.c): *pv NULL does nothing, w NULL clears *pv (no"] [1015 2 "// error), else *pv becomes bytes_concat's new bytes of the two buffers (a bytes-like object each, a C-contiguous"] [1016 2 "// one: anything else \"can't concat W to V\"), NULL on an error"] [1085 2 "// PyByteArray_Concat (Objects/bytearrayobject.c): a new bytearray of the two buffers (PyBUF_SIMPLE: a C-contiguous"] [1086 2 "// bytes-like object each, else \"can't concat B to A\")"] [1124 2 "// ---- str's core (Objects/unicodeobject.c) ----"] [1138 2 "// ensureStr is unicodeobject.c's ensure_unicode: an argument that is no str a TypeError \"must be str, not T\""] [1150 2 "// PyUnicode_GetLength and PyUnicode_ReadChar: an object that is no str is PyErr_BadArgument's TypeError; ReadChar's"] [1151 2 "// error is (Py_UCS4)-1, the 32-bit all-ones"] [1185 56 "// a subclass's instance: a new exact str (_PyUnicode_Copy)"] [1213 2 "// the str methods' natives: each str argument through ensure_unicode"] [1292 2 "// PyUnicode_Contains, Count, Find, FindChar and Tailmatch over the code points (their slices adjusted as"] [1293 2 "// ADJUST_INDICES does; a lone surrogate is a code point of its own)"] [1417 2 "// PyUnicode_EqualToUTF8 and EqualToUTF8AndSize: the str's strict UTF-8 (a surrogate never equal) against the size"] [1418 2 "// bytes, compared only when the sizes agree (no byte read past the str's own length)"] [1468 2 "// PyUnicode_AsXXXString and PyUnicode_AsEncodedString: an object that is no str is PyErr_BadArgument's TypeError"] [1500 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeXXX(const char *s, Py_ssize_t size, const char *errors)"] [1542 33 "// PyObject_GetBuffer(PyBUF_SIMPLE)"] [1548 2 "// ---- weak references (Objects/weakrefobject.c) ----"] [1572 2 "// ---- the module table (Python/import.c) ----"] [1601 2 "// PYC_MAGIC_NUMBER_TOKEN (Include/internal/pycore_magic_number.h: 3627, CPython 3.14's) as import.c gives it"] [1602 2 "// PyImport_GetMagicNumber (Python/import.c): the magic number of the interpreter's own importlib, its"] [1603 2 "// _bootstrap_external.MAGIC_NUMBER's four bytes as a little-endian long (pyi's, as importlib.util.MAGIC_NUMBER)"] [1635 2 "// PyImport_ImportModuleLevelObject (Python/import.c): name NULL is ValueError \"Empty module name\", a level < 0"] [1636 2 "// ValueError, a relative import's globals that are no dict TypeError \"globals must be a dict\" (resolve_name), then"] [1637 2 "// builtins.__import__'s own checks"] [1686 24 "// any hashable name (PyModule_NewObject keeps it as __name__)"] [1694 31 "// borrowed: sys.modules holds it"] [1707 2 "// ---- types (Objects/typeobject.c): every pyi type is ready; the cache is pyi's own"] [1712 3 "// a type object of C's memory (queue 269): a static PyTypeObject, or one C filled after type's tp_alloc"] [1719 2 "// ---- the codecs' stateful decoders (Objects/unicodeobject.c over _codecs' functions)"] [1721 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeUTF16(s, size, errors, int *byteorder) and its Stateful (..., Py_ssize_t *consumed)"] [1766 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeUTF8Stateful(s, size, errors, Py_ssize_t *consumed)"] [1799 2 "// PyUnicode_Translate is _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap: a code point the mapping lacks (LookupError) is kept, one it"] [1800 2 "// maps to None is undefined, given to the errors handler (str.translate deletes it)"] [1808 33 "// _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap's PyErr_BadArgument"] [1816 2 "// ---- files (Objects/fileobject.c) ----"] [1822 3 "// a bool warns (Objects/fileobject.c, 3.14; py-eval-1122: test_file's test_pyobject_asfiledescriptor)"] [1867 17 "// PyFile_WriteObject of NULL writes \"<NULL>\" (py-eval-1122: it was a Go panic)"] [1869 29 "// Py_PRINT_RAW"] [1940 2 "// ---- memory (Objects/obmalloc.c) ----"] [1944 2 "// PyMem_Calloc(nelem, elsize): zeroed (monitoring.c's CodeLike states; queue 274b)"] [1963 2 "// the inline accessors of the old limited versions, functions since 3.14's (Include/object.h)"] [1978 1 "// appendStr is PyUnicode_Append (PyObject **pleft, PyObject *right) and AppendAndDel."] [2011 1 "// cmpRunes is PyUnicode_Compare's order: by code point."] [2031 1 "// builtinMethod is a built-in type's method by name (list.sort)."] [2037 1 "// getargsKeywords is PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords (Python/getargs.c, vgetargskeywords): the positional arguments and the"] [2038 1 "// keywords of kwargs (nil: none) converted by format into the pointers, the parameters named by kwlist (a char *[] in"] [2039 1 "// the world, NULL-terminated; empty names are positional-only)."] [2125 5 "// PyDict_GetItemStringRef: the name decoded strictly (an invalid one is its UnicodeDecodeError; queue 270)"] [2158 63 "// skipitem leaves the format at the unit"] [2195 4 "// new_kwtuple: the keyword-capable names decoded strictly (an invalid one is its UnicodeDecodeError)"] [2204 27 "// (without _Py_CalculateSuggestions' \"Did you mean\")"] [2212 3 "// every extra keyword matched a name (a str subclass whose hash is not its text's: queue 270)"] [2222 1 "// replaceUTF8 is a C string as PyErr_Format's %s shows it: decoded from UTF-8 with errors \"replace\" (queue 270)."] [2232 1 "// parseKeywords is PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords's native."] [2255 1 "// addModule is PyImport_AddModuleRef: sys.modules[name], a new module put there when absent."] [2265 2 "// import_add_module: sys.modules' entry when it is a module; a lookup error but KeyError (an unhashable name)"] [2266 2 "// propagates"] [2290 14 "// PyModule_NewObject's __name__ is the name object as it is"] [2298 1 "// translateCharmap is unicodeobject.c's _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap over pyi's str."] [2332 3 "// the run of undefined characters goes to the handler"] [2386 1 "// maxAlloc is the largest size the C API's allocating natives try: above it CPython's allocator fails, a MemoryError"] [2387 1 "// (PyErr_NoMemory; PY_SSIZE_T_MAX's requests in test_capi)."] [2390 1 "// badArgument is PyErr_BadArgument's TypeError."] [2393 1 "// dictOf is a dict's storage when o is a dict or a dict subclass's instance (PyDict_Check)."] [2401 1 "// dictMerge is dictobject.c's dict_merge into d's storage (its own __setitem__ never called): b's entries read in"] [2402 1 "// place when b is a dict whose type keeps dict's __iter__ (a subclass's __getitem__ not called, as CPython's fast"] [2403 1 "// path), else through b.keys() and b[key]; an existing key is replaced only with override."] [2440 1 "// sameIter is t's __iter__ dict's own (tp_iter == dict_iter)."] [2450 1 "// adjustIndices is unicodeobject.c's ADJUST_INDICES: start and end as a slice's, within [0, n]."] [2472 1 "// runesFind is the first (dir > 0) or last occurrence of sub in s[lo:hi], an index of s, -1 when none; an empty sub is"] [2473 1 "// at lo (or hi)."] [2508 1 "// runesCount is the occurrences of sub in s[lo:hi], not overlapping (an empty sub hi-lo+1 times)."] [2528 1 "// voidPinned are the handles PyLong_FromVoidPtr gave as ints (each kept by one reference of its own)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[53 12] [53 19] [150 24] [156 35] [189 51] [206 51] [222 22] [296 32] [376 23] [377 35] [400 24] [425 52] [508 29] [523 32] [523 39] [529 29] [568 25] [606 23] [667 45] [747 25] [819 23] [945 26] [946 22] [1130 25] [1185 23] [1221 14] [1221 26] [1240 33] [1253 33] [1564 25] [1594 22] [1646 23] [1669 174] [1709 35] [1713 38] [1824 81] [19